# An ALLOWLIST: everything is ignored, then only what the image builds need
# is let back in (docker/Dockerfile, docker/web.Dockerfile,
# docker/media-delivery.Dockerfile).
#
# Never in the build context, whatever is added below: .env and every other
# secret file, web/.env.local (the deployment's brand), var/ and any media
# file, .git, node_modules, bin/, web/dist. The re-excludes at the end keep
# them out even inside an allowed directory.
*

# Go: module files and the code the binaries are built from.
!go.mod
!go.sum
!cmd/
!internal/
!migrations/

# web: what `pnpm install` and `pnpm build` read.
!web/package.json
!web/pnpm-lock.yaml
!web/pnpm-workspace.yaml
!web/index.html
!web/vite.config.ts
!web/tsconfig.json
!web/tsconfig.node.json
!web/security-headers.json
!web/public/
!web/src/
!web/scripts/

# nginx configs and the media-delivery start-up guard.
!docker/web/
!docker/nginx-media/default.conf.template
!docker/nginx-media/05-require-media-signing-key.sh

# Re-excluded everywhere, even under the directories above.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/*_test.go
**/testdata
**/*.mkv
**/*.mp4
**/*.mov
